{"uid":"44e07fca4ff0569f","name":"test_break_glass_apply_denies_when_persisted_evidence_has_gone_stale_since_earlier_checks","fullName":"tests.test_workspace_release_routes#test_break_glass_apply_denies_when_persisted_evidence_has_gone_stale_since_earlier_checks","historyId":"4fab65546b24df4349b41a0c944c8267","time":{"start":1792086118923,"stop":1792086118990,"duration":67},"description":"Proves the actual production wiring, not just the governance-layer\n    helper in isolation: build the identical verified QA->staging->prod\n    chain the success test above uses, then mutate the prod release's own\n    persisted evidence digest right before calling `_break_glass_apply_sync`\n    -- simulating evidence that went stale between an earlier read and the\n    apply itself. The route must re-derive live from the release row at call\n    time and deny, proving this is a real check and not a relocated\n    constant (the old hardcoded `True, True` would have let this through).\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Proves the actual production wiring, not just the governance-layer<br />\nhelper in isolation: build the identical verified QA-&gt;staging-&gt;prod<br />\nchain the success test above uses, then mutate the prod release's own<br />\npersisted evidence digest right before calling <code>_break_glass_apply_sync</code><br />\n-- simulating evidence that went stale between an earlier read and the<br />\napply itself. The route must re-derive live from the release row at call<br />\ntime and deny, proving this is a real check and not a relocated<br />\nconstant (the old hardcoded <code>True, True</code> would have let this through).</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1792084740901,"stop":1792084740902,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,